course: dictionary
lesson: 15457
title: Stimulating: a word that makes you think
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how something makes you feel or think. «Stimulating» is one of them. Something stimulating is interesting and exciting, and it makes your mind want to work and find out more.
explain: Look at the context: «Our science project was stimulating, because we got to test our own ideas.» The clues are test our own ideas and find out more. So stimulating means interesting in a way that makes you think. Check it by swapping in interesting: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The word can also mean making something more active. «The warm drink was stimulating his tired brain» means it made his brain more active. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Stimulating means interesting and exciting in a way that makes you think and want to know more.
fact: «Stimulating» can also mean making something more active, like a drink stimulating your brain.
fact: Stimulating is an adjective: more stimulating, most stimulating.
fact: Stimulating is also the -ing form of the verb stimulate. «They are stimulating growth» means they are making growth more active.
fact: Phrases you may see are «a stimulating discussion», «a stimulating classroom» and «intellectually stimulating».
exercise: «The museum visit was stimulating, and we asked the guide a hundred questions.» What does stimulating mean? | Boring and very long | *Interesting, so it made us want to find out more | Quiet and sleepy | Wet and muddy
exercise: «The hot drink was stimulating his tired brain.» What does stimulating mean here? | Cooling his brain down | Making his brain go to sleep | *Making his brain more active | Stopping his brain from working
exercise: Which would most likely be stimulating? | Waiting in a long queue | Watching paint dry | Sitting still with eyes closed | *A new science experiment that we design ourselves
test: «The new book was so stimulating that I read it in one night.» What does stimulating mean? | Wet and grey | *Exciting and interesting, making you want to know more | Dull and boring | Heavy to carry
test: «The scientists are stimulating the plants with light to help them grow.» What is the -ing word doing here? | *Making the plants more active | Covering the plants with sand | Cutting the plants down | Forgetting to water the plants
exam: Which best explains the meaning of stimulating in «The stimulating lesson made everyone ask questions»? | Made of wood | Short and rude | *Interesting and exciting, so pupils wanted to think and ask | Boring and quiet
